Go, Crocodilus!

254
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:50,357
Battling me won't bring your brother back.

255
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:53,017
And we want to stop
Pegasus as much as you do.

256
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:54,897
He's taken my grandfather prisoner.

257
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:55,810
That's right.

258
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:57,437
Pegasus is the bad guy here.

259
00:13:57,520 --> 00:13:59,397
Can't you see that, you crazy little kid?

260
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:00,310
You're wrong.

261
00:14:00,393 --> 00:14:02,097
I have to protect my brother's company,

262
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:05,945
and Yugi's the one Pegasus has
to beat in order to take it over.

263
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,380
Wait, I get it.

264
00:14:07,780 --> 00:14:12,017
Mokuba is trying to save his brother's
company by defeating Yugi in a duel,

265
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:14,597
so Pegasus doesn't get
to face Yugi at all.

266
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:15,680
What do you mean?

267
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:17,437
What do you mean, what do I mean?

268
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:18,980
I wasn't talking to you.

269
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:21,265
Sorry, what did you mean, Pea?

270
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:24,657
If Mokuba can keep
Pegasus from beating Yugi,

271
00:14:24,740 --> 00:14:27,257
then he won't be able to
take over Kaiba's company.

272
00:14:27,340 --> 00:14:28,516
Ah, that must be it.

273
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:31,380
Hey, where'd he go?

274
00:14:31,660 --> 00:14:36,000
If I can't beat you, I'll be
disqualified. My start shifts.

275
00:14:38,300 --> 00:14:39,771
Hold up, you little punk.

276
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:41,820
Mokuba, listen to me.

277
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:44,567
You'll never save Kaiba
Corporation that way.

278
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:47,660
Your big brother is just confused.

279
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:50,997
After I defeated Kaiba in
our duel, I opened his mind.

280
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:54,657
I removed from him all the dark
influences that clouded his thoughts.

281
00:14:54,740 --> 00:15:00,237
and actions free of that evil essence
kaiba is struggling now your brother

282
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:03,697
realizes that his way wasn't the
right way and he's searching his heart

283
00:15:03,780 --> 00:15:07,517
for answers and you know in your heart
what you're doing isn't the right way

284
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:14,300
either but then what can i do you can
start by trusting in me and together

285
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:19,137
we will defeat pegasus
i promise you we can

286
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:21,808
only bring pegasus down
if we stick together

287
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:25,237
We'll help you protect your brother,
Mokuba, but you've got to help us, okay?

288
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:27,297
You've got to go back
and return those cards

289
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:29,977
and star chips to the
kid you stole them from.

290
00:15:30,060 --> 00:15:31,178
You're right, Yugi.

291
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:33,597
Then we'll take on Pegasus together.

292
00:15:33,680 --> 00:15:36,097
We've only got three minutes
left till the boat leaves.

293
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:37,592
Let's get going, Mokuba.

294
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:40,060
Let's do it.

295
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:44,680
It's no use.

296
00:15:44,900 --> 00:15:49,077
I've gone over it a dozen times in my
mind, but I still can't figure it out.

297
00:15:49,160 --> 00:15:53,337
How was a kid who came out of nowhere
able to defeat a champion like me?

298
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:55,185
I've run computer simulations,

299
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:56,754
probability scenarios,

300
00:15:56,940 --> 00:16:00,837
and quantum analysis of our duel,
but I still don't have the answer.

301
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:03,273
I had clearly been dominating the match.

302
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:06,579
My blue-eyes white dragon
ripped through his forces.

303
00:16:07,940 --> 00:16:09,705
I was on the verge of winning.

304
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:11,480
But Yugi wouldn't give up.

305
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:15,357
Against all odds and with absolute
faith in his grandfather's deck,

306
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:18,616
he somehow drew the one card
that assured his victory.

307
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:20,720
Exodia, it's not possible!

308
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,358
Exodia, obliterate!

309
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:33,737
I've always believed Duel Monsters
was a game of sheer power,

310
00:16:33,820 --> 00:16:36,408
but Yugi claims that
the cards have a heart.

311
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:41,980
It sounds crazy, I know,
but could Yugi be right?

312
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:45,797
Is there really a heart of the cards
that can affect the outcome of a duel?

313
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:46,817
Is that how he won?

314
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:49,837
The only way I'll know for
sure is to face Yugi again.

315
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:52,257
And these new portable
holo-generators will enable

316
00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:54,457
me to challenge him no
matter where I find him.

317
00:16:54,540 --> 00:16:56,300
If I can just get to...

318
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:57,737
Settle, Kaiba.

319
00:16:57,820 --> 00:16:59,017
We know you're in there.

320
00:16:59,100 --> 00:17:01,276
Open the door or we'll break it down.

321
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:03,640
Let's go, Kaiba.

322
00:17:04,020 --> 00:17:05,840
On your feet. Mr.

323
00:17:06,180 --> 00:17:09,004
Pegasus would like to
have a few words with you.

324
00:17:09,260 --> 00:17:13,142
I bet he would, but it'll take
more than you two goons to grab me.

325
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:17,420
This can go easy, or we can
snap you in two. Wise guy.

326
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:19,128
You'll never take me alive.

327
00:17:20,240 --> 00:17:21,070
Get him.

328
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:24,320
He jumped.

329
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:27,875
Nobody could survive a fall like that.

330
00:17:28,140 --> 00:17:30,500
Looks like he did our work for us.

331
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:33,409
Yeah, that just leaves
the rest of the job.

332
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:35,857
Pegasus was very clear.

333
00:17:35,940 --> 00:17:39,234
He wants to deck with the
deadly Blue-Eyes White Dragon.

334
00:17:48,820 --> 00:17:50,349
Hurry, we're almost there.

335
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:53,380
We're gonna just make it. What?

336
00:17:53,580 --> 00:17:57,700
I told you I'm not gonna row,
so quit bugging me! The boat.

337
00:17:57,860 --> 00:17:59,000
It's already left.

338
00:17:59,220 --> 00:18:02,297
And there's the sleazy low
light that shipped them out.

339
00:18:02,380 --> 00:18:03,321
You're too late.

340
00:18:03,460 --> 00:18:05,597
Those losers are on their way back home.

341
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:07,300
Hey, that's not fair.

342
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:09,304
It hasn't been a half hour yet.

343
00:18:09,620 --> 00:18:10,450
Tough luck.

344
00:18:10,533 --> 00:18:13,020
Pegasus sets the schedule here. That's it.

345
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:14,905
I'm gonna give you a flat top.

346
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:16,657
You've got to call the boat back.

347
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:19,564
I've got to return that
kid's star chips to him.

348
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:21,380
The star chips!

349
00:18:24,040 --> 00:18:24,960
What gives?

350
00:18:25,260 --> 00:18:28,177
A bunch of those star chips
belong to Yugi, you big joke.

351
00:18:28,260 --> 00:18:30,180
I am so sorry, Yugi.

352
00:18:30,940 --> 00:18:35,234
You losers should keep a tighter grip
on your valuables, don't you think?

353
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:37,852
Then accidents like that wouldn't happen.

354
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:40,940
Now, let's go, you.

355
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:42,030
Back to the cage.

356
00:18:42,113 --> 00:18:44,880
This little ingrate is
a special guest of Mr.

357
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:46,317
Maximillian Pegasus,

358
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:50,877
and he's been invited to attend a special
dinner in his honor back at the castle.

359
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:51,840
Right, Mokuba?

360
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,260
Yugi! Hold on.

361
00:18:54,820 --> 00:18:55,650
Hmm?

362
00:18:55,733 --> 00:18:58,112
I still have three of my star chips left.

363
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:02,607
I challenge you to a duel, and
if I win, Mokuba comes with us.

364
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:03,950
Hmm.

365
00:19:04,033 --> 00:19:06,477
I don't know why you'd risk
your chips for this punk,

366
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:09,197
but if that's how you want to
waste your last star chips,

367
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:13,260
Then meet me back at Arena
146 in exactly four hours.

368
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:14,774
You'll have your duel.

369
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:15,977
Well, we're here.

370
00:19:16,060 --> 00:19:17,295
Where's Antenna Head?

371
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:21,560
Yugi, over here!

372
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:23,560
Get him off me!

373
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:26,000
Mokuba, put him down now.

374
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:28,400
I'll consider it if you win the duel.

375
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:30,097
Oh, I'll beat you, all right.

376
00:19:30,180 --> 00:19:31,709
I never said I would duel.

377
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:33,473
There is your opponent.

378
00:19:33,740 --> 00:19:36,564
He's an old friend who's
dying to see you again.

379
00:19:36,820 --> 00:19:39,197
He met with an unfortunate
end earlier today.

380
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:41,720
but he's come back just to duel you.

381
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,176
What are you saying?

382
00:19:45,360 --> 00:19:46,190
Kaiba?

383
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:47,380
Yes, Yugi.

384
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:49,580
It's me, Kaiba.

385
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:53,600
And this time you don't
stand a ghost of a chance.
